                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Agitation; the state of being perturbed"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14c74d05-8010-43da-b239-f87ab589e392",
                                                "sense_id": "a012baba-1a5e-349e-89e6-d0728b8cc31c",
                                                "text": "Reſtore your ſelues, vnto your temper, Fathers; / And, vvithout perturbation, heare me ſpeake: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8bd2c34-d3aa-4806-898d-21e692099e23",
                                                "sense_id": "a012baba-1a5e-349e-89e6-d0728b8cc31c",
                                                "text": "But her mind had never been in such perturbation; and it needed a very strong effort to appear attentive and cheerful till the usual hour of separating allowed her the relief of quiet reflection."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5844aef4-d18f-3d99-b74c-e2e52b05ee3c",
                                        "entry_id": "54a0c1a4-9a4c-3bec-8e6d-07f7c700aca8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small change in a physical system, or more broadly any definable system (such as a biological or economic system)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff5b46e4-2d4a-4c40-886a-88f0fb8941a6",
                                                "sense_id": "5844aef4-d18f-3d99-b74c-e2e52b05ee3c",
                                                "text": "Natures that haue much Heat, and great and violent deſires and Perturbations, are not ripe for Action, till they haue paſſed the Meridian of their yeares: As it was with Iulius Cæſar, and Septimius Seuerus."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
